From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Taozuhong <taozuhong@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Oct 2026 02:30:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] MinGW: make IPC serialization manifests' platform variants
 mutually exclusive

Update 37 (fixing the round-36 CLANG64/CLANGARM64
WebKitPlatformGeneratedSerializers.cpp 10-error block at [8504|8460]/8564;
UCRT64 still stalls at [7041] Linking CXX static library libSkia.a - a
separate issue addressed by the PKGBUILD llvm-ar change of this round).

CI errors (identical on CLANG64 and CLANGARM64, WebKitPlatformGeneratedSerializers.cpp):

  :91   error: static assertion failed due to requirement
        'std::is_same_v<WTF::UnixFileDescriptor, WTF::Win32Handle>'
  :101  error: duplicate member 'm_handle' (Win32Handle vs previous UnixFileDescriptor)
  :107  error: static assertion failed: sizeof(ShouldBeSameSizeAsConnectionHandle)
        == sizeof(IPC::ConnectionHandle) evaluates '1 == 8'
  :137  error: redefinition of 'm_handle' (decoder.decode<Win32Handle> vs
        previous decoder.decode<UnixFileDescriptor>)
  :145  error: no matching constructor for 'IPC::ConnectionHandle' (2 arguments
        provided - both the USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) and the OS(WINDOWS) branch
        of the braced initializer list are active)
  ... and the same five errors again for WebCore::SharedMemoryHandle at
  :6655/:6666/:6670/:6723/:6738 (3 arguments vs SharedMemoryHandle(Type&&, uint64_t)).

Root cause: the .serialization.in manifests declare the platform-specific
m_handle member as three INDEPENDENT #if blocks:

  #if USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
      UnixFileDescriptor m_handle;
  #endif
  #if OS(WINDOWS)
      Win32Handle m_handle;
  #endif
  #if OS(DARWIN)
      MachSendRight m_handle;
  #endif

generate-serializers.py parses each #if expression verbatim into
member.condition and emits every member variant as its own #if block
(static_assert, ShouldBeSameSizeAs member, IsIncreasing/offsetof entry,
encode statement, decode local, constructor initializer - 6 emission
sites per variant). On every upstream platform at most one of these
conditions is true, so the independent #ifs happen to be exclusive.
On MinGW GTK both USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) (PlatformUse.h defines it
unconditionally for PLATFORM(GTK)||PLATFORM(WPE), even on Windows) and
OS(WINDOWS) are true simultaneously, and the generated
WebKitPlatformGeneratedSerializers.cpp becomes ill-formed.

The real C++ headers (ConnectionHandle.h:53-82, SharedMemory.h Type alias
and private members) already model this correctly with a #if/#elif/#elif
chain in which USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS) takes precedence; that is why the
headers themselves compile fine on MinGW GTK and only the GENERATED
serializers break. IPCSemaphore.serialization.in hit the same class of
problem in round 27 and was fixed with the identical
`OS(WINDOWS) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)` pattern.

Fix: make the manifest variants mirror the headers' #elif semantics by
excluding the unix flavor from the other two variants:

  #if OS(WINDOWS) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
  #if OS(DARWIN) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)

This is a no-op on every upstream platform (Linux GTK/WPE: OS(WINDOWS)=0,
OS(DARWIN)=0; Cocoa: USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)=0 so the DARWIN/WINDOWS
conditions keep their original value; WinCairo: USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)=0)
and only changes behavior for the MinGW GTK combination, where the unix
flavor now wins - exactly matching the headers the generated code is
asserted against.

Files touched (no existing patch touches either file):

  Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/ConnectionHandle.serialization.in
  Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in (SharedMemoryHandle)

Verification (Linux sandbox, generator + compile-shape methodology of
rounds 27-36):

1. Generator-level: ran Scripts/generate-serializers.py over all 329
   .serialization.in manifests of the patched tree (split-by-directory
   mode, same invocation the CMake custom command uses). PRE vs POST
   diff of ALL generated outputs (WebKitPlatformGeneratedSerializers.cpp,
   SerializedTypeInfo.cpp and every per-bundle file) shows exactly 28
   changed lines - every emitted `#if OS(WINDOWS)` / `#if OS(DARWIN)`
   guard of the two types' variants gains `&& !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)`;
   nothing else changes.

2. Compile-shape matrix (g++ -std=c++23 -fsyntax-only, verbatim-extracted
   encode/decode blocks from the real generated file, real-class stubs
   mirroring ConnectionHandle.h / SharedMemory.h member layout, real
   wtf/IsIncreasing.h):

     PRE  + MinGW GTK (UNIX=1,WINDOWS=1)  -> FAIL, reproducing every CI
                                             error class (static_assert
                                             is_same failure, duplicate
                                             m_handle member, redefinition
                                             of auto m_handle, no matching
                                             constructor for the 2-arg /
                                             3-arg braced initializers)
     PRE  + Linux GTK  (UNIX=1)           -> PASS
     POST + MinGW GTK  (UNIX=1,WINDOWS=1) -> PASS   <-- fix target
     POST + Linux GTK  (UNIX=1)           -> PASS   (no regression)
     POST + WinCairo   (UNIX=0,WINDOWS=1) -> PASS   (no regression)
     POST + Darwin     (UNIX=0,DARWIN=1)  -> PASS   (no regression)

3. Scope sweep: grepped all 329 manifests for platform-conditioned
   members. Only ConnectionHandle and SharedMemoryHandle carry the
   USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)/OS(WINDOWS) dual-true combination
   (IPCSemaphore was fixed in round 27; the ProcessID `using` aliases in
   WTFArgumentCoders/WebCoreArgumentCoders are #if/#else and match the
   real wtf/ProcessID.h on MinGW; SharedFileHandle is COCOA-only;
   TestSerializedType.serialization.in is the generator's own unit-test
   fixture and is not part of the CMake build).
---
 .../IPC/ConnectionHandle.serialization.in         | 4 ++--
 .../WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in        | 4 ++--
 2 files changed, 4 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/ConnectionHandle.serialization.in b/Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/ConnectionHandle.serialization.in
--- a/Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/ConnectionHandle.serialization.in
+++ b/Source/WebKit/Platform/IPC/ConnectionHandle.serialization.in
@@ -25,10 +25,10 @@ webkit_platform_header: "ConnectionHandle.h"
 #if USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
     UnixFileDescriptor m_handle;
 #endif
-#if OS(WINDOWS)
+#if OS(WINDOWS) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
     Win32Handle m_handle;
 #endif
-#if OS(DARWIN)
+#if OS(DARWIN) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
     MachSendRight m_handle;
 #endif
 }
diff --git a/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in b/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in
--- a/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in
+++ b/Source/WebKit/Shared/WebCoreArgumentCoders.serialization.in
@@ -1661,10 +1661,10 @@ headers: <WebCore/SharedMemory.h>
 #if USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
     [Validator='!!m_handle && *m_handle'] UnixFileDescriptor m_handle;
 #endif
-#if OS(DARWIN)
+#if OS(DARWIN) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
     [Validator='!!m_handle && *m_handle'] MachSendRight m_handle;
 #endif
-#if OS(WINDOWS)
+#if OS(WINDOWS) && !USE(UNIX_DOMAIN_SOCKETS)
     [Validator='!!m_handle && *m_handle'] Win32Handle m_handle;
 #endif
     uint64_t m_size;
--
2.47.0

